# less binds arrow/Home/End from terminfo, and xterm-256color defines only the
# application-cursor forms (kcud1=\EOB). A terminal that ignores less's DECCKM
# request (\e[?1h) keeps sending the normal-mode CSI forms, which less has no
# binding for, so it just beeps. Bind those forms too.

#command
\e[A            back-line
\e[B            forw-line
\e[C            right-scroll
\e[D            left-scroll
\e[H            goto-line
\e[F            goto-end
\e[1~           goto-line
\e[4~           goto-end
